From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Menno <menno@localhost>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] qmi: support AFW position reports without modem NMEA

Newer Snapdragon GNSS engines reject LOC Start with GENERAL_FAILURE unless
the same LOC client first registers as an application-framework client.  Send
the identity TLVs added in libqmi 1.38.0_git20261005 and move event
registration before LOC Start.  Retain the identity on the assistance event
registration too.

Some Qualcomm firmware accepts that authenticated session but emits position
reports instead of the requested NMEA indications.  Subscribe to those reports
and convert successful latitude/longitude fixes into GGA sentences for
ModemManager's existing GPS raw, NMEA and location-cache paths.
---
 src/mm-shared-qmi.c | 99 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++------------------
 1 file changed, 60 insertions(+), 39 deletions(-)

